 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::command` executes a backend-native command against an existing session using the
+  raw slash-prefixed chat input. Providers that do not expose selected-session commands use the
+  default unsupported-command error instead of receiving that input through the ordinary prompt path.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
@@ -651,10 +654,11 @@ New agent-provider support follows this path:
 
 1. Define an `AgentProfile` with `AgentKind::External`.
 2. Implement `AgentBackend` for the provider.
-3. Override streaming methods when the provider can emit real-time output.
-4. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
-5. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
-6. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
+3. Override `AgentBackend::command` when the provider exposes native selected-session commands.
+4. Override streaming methods when the provider can emit real-time output.
+5. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
+6. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
+7. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
 
 `AgentBackend::session` is an optional session snapshot hook. Work Leaf tracks hidden system-agent
 initialization itself, so provider implementations do not need to override `session` for persistent
@@ -662,7 +666,7 @@ initialization itself, so provider implementations do not need to override `sess
 
 New core workflow behavior belongs in the workflow module that owns the behavior. UI adapters should
 only translate user input into controller calls and render controller snapshots. Agent providers
-should only implement launch, send, streaming, and shutdown behavior.
+should only implement launch, send, command, streaming, and shutdown behavior.
 
 ## API and Architecture Change Policy
 
